COPY nebula.agent_records_history (id, record_type, role, title, content, source_path, metadata, tags, system_id, subsystem_id, feature_id, plan_ref, created_at, updated_at, as_of_dt, expiration_dt) FROM stdin;
7fbb38a0-ffab-4256-809c-42c835beffcc	architecture_note	architect	Implementation Plan: Conduit UI Modernization	# Implementation Plan: Conduit UI Modernization\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nConduit UI has fallen out of sync with the other Nexus applications being pulled into nexus-console via iframe (nebula-ui, duality, plurality). It has three categories of issues: (1) visual design mismatch, (2) plans display broken from DB-only plans, (3) tool call errors flooding the UI. This plan addresses all three.\n\n---\n\n## Issue 1: Visual Design Mismatch\n\n### Current State\n- Conduit UI uses pure CSS custom properties for theming (no Tailwind)\n- Emoji icons for navigation (house, clipboard, construction, magnifying glass, etc.)\n- Horizontal tab bar at top\n- Dark/light theme via CSS vars in styles.scss (500+ lines)\n- Inline templates and inline styles (angular.json config)\n- Angular 19 with standalone components\n\n### Reference Apps\n- **Nebula UI** (Angular 21): Tailwind CSS, vertical sidebar with SVG icon buttons, dark mode via Tailwind dark: variants, separate template files\n- **Plurality UI** (React + Vite): Tailwind CSS, modern React patterns\n- **Nexus Console**: Angular with separate CSS files, tree-view and service-graph components\n- **Duality**: Angular with SCSS component files, header/footer pattern\n\n### Required Changes\n\n1. **Add Tailwind CSS** to conduit-ui package.json\n   - Add tailwindcss dependency\n   - Configure tailwind.config.js\n   - Update src/styles.scss to use @tailwind directives\n   - Enables theme-class consistency with nebula-ui\n\n2. **Replace emoji icons with SVG icons**\n   - Use Heroicons or inline SVG paths (matching nebula-ui approach)\n   - Update all components currently using emoji icons\n\n3. **Replace horizontal nav tabs with vertical sidebar**\n   - Current: div.nav-tabs with inline a tags\n   - Target: vertical sidebar matching nebula-ui w-14 view-switcher pattern\n   - Add active state styling with SVG highlight\n   - Reposition theme toggle, chat, config buttons into sidebar\n\n4. **Update color palette and theme system**\n   - Either adopt Tailwind theme fully\n   - Or align CSS vars with nebula-ui palette (blue-600, gray-900, etc.)\n\n---\n\n## Issue 2: Plans Display Not Showing DB-Only Plans\n\n### Current State\n- conduit-mcp watcher loads plans from DB via getPlansGroupedByStatus()\n- plan-watcher.ts calls loadFromDb() during initialize()\n- getState() queries DB fresh each time via getPlansGroupedByStatus()\n- Plans stored in conduit.plans table with derived status from receipts\n- conduit-ui connects via SSE to /events for initial + incremental state\n\n### Root Causes\n\n1. **SSE event plan_state_changed triggers refetch but plan-watcher cache may be stale**\n   - plan-watcher.loadFromDb() only runs once during initialize()\n   - The in-memory cache in planWatcher.plans is not refreshed\n   - However, getState() calls getPlansGroupedByStatus() fresh from DB, bypassing the cache\n\n2. **Potential empty state if conduit-mcp was restarted**\n   - Conduit schema tables (plans, receipts, tickets) are separate from nebula schema\n   - SCD Type 4 migration only touched nebula schema -- conduit plans unaffected\n   - If conduit-mcp server is running and connected, plans should be accessible\n\n3. **Need to verify DB state**\n   - Check if conduit.plans table has rows\n   - Check if conduit.receipts table has rows\n   - Run SELECT COUNT(*) FROM conduit.plan_status to verify view returns data\n\n### Required Changes\n\n1. **Add periodic DB plan refresh to plan-watcher**\n   - loadFromDb() only runs during initialize()\n   - Add a periodic refresh (every 30s) so new plans appear without SSE\n\n2. **Add DB health diagnostics to /health endpoint**\n   - Report plan count, receipt count, ticket count\n   - Report DB connection status\n\n---\n\n## Issue 3: Tool Call Errors Flooding the UI\n\n### Current State\n- error.interceptor.ts catches ALL HTTP errors and displays via GlobalErrorService\n- Many tool calls are best-effort but still trigger error banners\n- Interceptor has timeout(15000) + retry({ count: 1, delay: 1000 })\n\n### Root Causes\n\n1. **Interceptor fires BEFORE component catch block**\n   - RxJS error flow: request -> retry(1) -> catchError(interceptor) -> throwError -> component\n   - globalError.show() runs before re-throwing\n   - Even component-level error handling can't suppress the global banner\n\n2. **Some endpoints consistently fail**\n   - /chat/config returns errors when agent chat server is not running\n   - /tools/call with query_prompts fails if PROMPTS directory doesn't exist\n   - /config/cron may fail on older servers\n\n### Required Changes\n\n1. **Add error categorization to the interceptor**\n   - Distinguish between operational errors (expected) and actionable errors (show banner)\n   - Use URL pattern matching to suppress non-critical endpoints\n\n2. **Increase timeouts**\n   - From 15s to 30s for tool calls\n   - Reduce retry count from 1 to 0 for non-idempotent operations\n\n---\n\n## Issue 4: Additional Out-of-Date Features\n\n- conduit.service.ts returns empty arrays for prompts, inspections, change reports (filesystem artifacts not read back)\n- Archive browser, inspection dashboard, prompt catalog, changes view may show no data\n- Session log SSE streaming still works (filesystem fallback)\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n### Phase 1: Fix Functional Issues (Week 1)\n1. Debug and fix plans display -- verify DB state, fix plan-watcher refresh\n2. Fix error interceptor to suppress non-critical errors\n3. Add DB health diagnostics to /health endpoint\n\n### Phase 2: Visual Redesign (Week 2)\n4. Add Tailwind CSS to conduit-ui\n5. Redesign navigation: horizontal tabs to vertical sidebar with SVG icons\n6. Update color palette and theme system to match nebula-ui\n\n### Phase 3: Polish (Week 3)\n7. Replace remaining emoji icons across all components\n8. Clean up inline styles to consistent Tailwind classes\n9. Test all views and fix empty-state displays\n10. Run conduit-ui alongside other apps in nexus-console iframe\n\n---\n\n## Success Criteria\n- Plans display correctly in the Planner view (loaded from DB)\n- No spurious error banners on page load\n- Visual appearance matches other apps (sidebar, SVG icons, Tailwind)\n- All tool calls work without flooding UI with errors\n- Conduit UI looks cohesive alongside nebula-ui and plurality UI in nexus-console	\N	{"author": "architect", "status": "proposed", "priority": "high", "estimatedEffort": "2-3 weeks", "affectedServices": ["conduit-ui", "conduit-mcp"]}	{implementation-plan,conduit-ui,phase-2,visual-redesign,database-first}	\N	\N	\N	\N	2026-06-21 22:27:04.610748+00	2026-06-21 22:27:04.610748+00	2026-06-21 22:27:04.610748+00	9999-12-31 23:59:59+00
