nd execution. It appears in the Lowering Pass, Execution Graph Schema, Phase 2 Runtime, and Validator. | File | Relationship | | --- | --- | | LOWERING\\_PASS.md | §5.11: Step 8 - Freeze. Graph topology locked after validation | | EXECUTION\\_GRAPH\\_SCHEMA.md | §3.1: Immutable topology rule - only lifecycle\\_state, outputs, event\\_refs MAY mutate | | PHASE2\\_EXECUTION\\_RUNTIME.md | §2: Frozen ExecutionGraph as input to scheduler | | COMPILER\\_ARCHITECTURE.md | §4.3: Output must be frozen (topology immutable) | | VALIDATOR\\_SPEC.md | S9: Frozen Topology Rule - mutability flag | 36. Snapshots as Derived Compression Phrase reuse: "snapshot", "derived compression", "deletable, regenerable", "fast replay start", "NOT canonical truth" Snapshots are explicitly NOT canonical truth - they are derived compression artifacts of CER history. This framing appears in CER\\_SPEC, CER\\_SNAPSHOT\\_ENGINE, and REPLAY\\_ENGINE. | File | Relationship | | --- | --- | | CER\\_SNAPSHOT\\_ENGINE.md | Canonical definition - trigger model, triple-version lock | | CER\\_SPEC.md | §5: Snapshot Triggers (4 conditions) | | REPLAY\\_ENGINE.md | §8: Snapshot Model - derived compression, not checkpoints | | CER\\_CCNF.md | §12: Version Anchoring - snapshot validity requires triple-version lock | | CCNF\\_FAILURE\\_MODES.md | FM#9: Version Skew - triple-version lock enforcement | | DISTRIBUTED\\_SCHEDULER.md | §17.1: Snapshots provide fast incremental replay |\n\nShow more Show less\n\n#### ChatGPT said:\n\nWhat you've added here actually tightens the system a lot-you're no longer just defining layers, you're converging on a *coherent lattice of interpretation → structure → execution → observation → identity* .\n\nIf I normalize what you've got, IRL/IRL-adjacent + compiler + runtime + observation + identity all collapse into a single pipeline with two orthogonal axes:\n\n- **Axis 1: epistemic classification (what kind of thing is this?)**\n- **Axis 2: structural transformation (what does it become in the system?)**\n\n# 1. The missing unifier: IRL ↔ IR bridge\n\nYou now have:\n\n- **IRL (probabilistic):** "what is this interaction likely to be?"\n- **IR (deterministic):** "what interaction contract is legally allowed?"\n\nThat pairing is actually a classic:\n\nIRL = Bayesian observer over interaction space\nIR = type system over interaction space\n\nSo the clean relationship is:\n\n```\nUser Input  ↓  IRL (probabilistic classification: soft labels)  ↓  Interaction Taxonomy Resolver  ↓  IR (deterministic archetype selection: hard constraint)  ↓  Authority Graph mutation rules (VALIDATOR_SPEC)\n```\n\nKey point: **IRL never decides structure. It only proposes probability mass over IR types.**\n\nThat preserves your "closed contract" idea cleanly.\n\n# 2. Your system is actually 5-phase, not 4-phase\n\nYour compiler/runtime/observation split is solid, but with IRL + IR included, the real pipeline is:\n\n## Phase 0 - Interaction Semantics Layer (NEW: IRL/IR)\n\n- nexus\\_irl\\_taxonomy.md (probabilistic classification)\n- nexus\\_interaction\\_taxonomy.md (deterministic contract)\n- VALIDATOR\\_SPEC.md (enforcement gate)\n\n👉 Output: *Validated Interaction Intent Vector*\n\n## Phase 1 - Specification Compiler\n\n(PHASE1\\_SPECIFICATION\\_COMPILER.md)\n\n- Prompt → WorkRequestGraph\n- structural decomposition\n- semantic normalization\n\n👉 Output: WorkRequestGraph\n\n## Phase 1.5 - Lowering Pass\n\n- WorkRequestGraph → ExecutionGraph\n- freeze boundary defined here\n\n👉 Output: Frozen ExecutionGraph\n\n## Phase 2 - Execution Runtime\n\n(PHASE2\\_EXECUTION\\_RUNTIME.md)\n\n- deterministic scheduler\n- CER event emission\n- append-only log writes\n\n👉 Output: Event stream + state transitions\n\n## Phase 3 - Observation Model\n\n(OBSERVATION\\_MODEL.md)\n\n- projection layer\n- replay + derived views\n- ephemeral semantics\n\n👉 Output: semantic projections\n\n## Phase 4 - Identity / Persistence Layer (cross-cutting)\n\n(CER\\_SPEC, AUTHORITY\\_GRAPH\\_IR, entity\\_key system)\n\nThis is NOT a runtime phase-it is a *global invariant system* :\n\n- append-only log integrity\n- identity collapse\n- deterministic replay\n- snapshot compression rules\n\n# 3. The real backbone: 4 invariants that unify everything\n\nYour system is actually held together by four invariants that show up everywhere:\n\n## (A) Determinism\n\nsame input → same output\n\nThis binds:\n\n- compiler\n- runtime\n- replay engine\n- validator\n\n## (B) Append-only truth model\n\nevents are facts, never mutated\n\nThis binds:\n\n- CER\n- scheduler\n- event grammar\n- distributed replay\n\n## (C) Freeze boundary\n\ntopology is immutable after lowering\n\nThis separates:\n\n- "planning world"\n- "execution world"\n\n## (D) Identity collapse (entity\\_key system)\n\nall entities resolve to stable canonical signatures\n\nThis binds:\n\n- observation\n- distributed scheduler\n- replay engine\n- snapshot system\n\n# *4. What IRL/IR actually adds (important insight)*\n\nBefore IRL/IR, your system starts at:\n\n"we already know what kind of interaction this is"\n\nBut IRL introduces:\n\n### probabilistic ambiguity handling BEFORE commitment\n\nThat gives you:\n\n- soft classification of intent drift\n- multi-hypothesis WorkRequest generation\n- better routing into compiler front-end\n\nSo IRL is not decoration-it is:\n\nthe *uncertainty buffer* between language and structure\n\n# 5. The real architecture collapse (clean form)\n\nIf I compress everything into a single diagram:\n\n```\n┌────────────────────┐  │   IRL (Bayes)      │  │ probabilistic tags │  └────────┬───────────┘  ↓  ┌────────────────────┐  │ IR (contracts)     │  │ deterministic type │  └────────┬───────────┘  ↓  ┌──────────────────────────────────┐  │ PHASE 1: SPEC COMPILER           │  │ Prompt → WorkRequestGraph        │  └────────┬─────────────────────────┘  ↓  ┌──────────────────────────────────┐  │ LOWERING PASS (FREEZE)           │  │ WorkRequest → ExecutionGraph     │ 