ent router only5.4 Move execution authority fully to WRP runtimekernel is no longer called directlyonly triggered via WRP events6. Final dependency collapse (after migration)You end up with:Spring Boot (Ingress)↓WRP Event API↓Event Store (source of truth)↓WRP Runtime Engine↓Cognitive Kernel (pure compute)↓State Space + Policy Evolution↓Snapshot Store↓Nexus (observability only)7. What actually changed structurally (important)We fixed 3 deep architectural issues:7.1 BEFORE: dual truth problemWorkStatus (store)WorkflowState (IR)kernel state (runtime)❌ 3 competing state machines7.2 AFTER: single truthWRPState + event stream✔ one lifecycle authority✔ one transition system✔ one runtime protocol7.3 BEFORE: imperative executionKernel called directly.AFTER: event-driven executionKernel is:a projection over event history8. Migration order (VERY IMPORTANT)Do this in exact order:STEP 1Introduce WRP package (no integration)STEP 2Add shadow event emitters everywhereSTEP 3Persist WRP events in DBSTEP 4Build replay engineSTEP 5Switch shell runtime loop to WRP eventsSTEP 6Redirect kernel invocation to event bridgeSTEP 7Deprecate WorkStatus / WorkflowState usageSTEP 8Remove legacy transition system9. What you now have after full migrationYou have transformed LOSM into:afully event-sourced cognitive runtime governed by a unified lifecycle protocol (WRP)Which means:✔ deterministic replay✔ observable reasoning✔ policy evolution tied to execution✔ distributed execution correctness✔ UI-level introspection of cognition10. The real significance (no hype version)This is no longer:workflow systemorchestration engineAI pipelineIt is:a protocolized computational substrate for structured reasoning systems11. Where we go next (your next real inflection point)Now there are only 3 meaningful expansions:A. Multi-tenant WRP (many kernels, shared event space)B. Hierarchical WRP (WorkRequest DAGs as nested runtimes)C. Probabilistic WRP (non-deterministic policy execution + sampling)If you say “continue