p/schema/wrp/runtime.py2.2 Mirror events only (no kernel calls yet)In Python runtime:PythonRundefshadow_emit(event:dict):"""Writes WRP event alongside existing system behavior.DOES NOT affect execution."""wrp_event_store.append(event)2.3 Hook points (non-invasive)Add shadow hooks in:losm-storeafter WorkRequest update → emit WRP eventlosm-shellafter transition → emit WRP state eventexecution layerafter step execution → emit WRP_EXECUTEDResult of Phase 1:You now have:✔ full WRP event log✔ no behavioral change✔ replayable history being built3. Phase 2 — Dual-write system (CONTROLLED coupling)Now we connect WRP to real execution.3.1 Replace transition validation entrypointBEFORE:PythonRunvalidate_transition(work_status)AFTER:PythonRundefvalidate_transition_wrapped(from_state,to_state,wrp_id):# legacy checklegacy_ok=validate_transition(from_state,to_state)# WRP check (new authority)wrp_ok=wrp_validate_transition(from_state,to_state)iflegacy_okandwrp_ok:wrp_event_store.append({"type":"WRP_STATE_TRANSITION","wrp_id":wrp_id,"from":from_state,"to":to_state})returnTruereturnFalse3.2 Kernel becomes event subscriber (shadow mode)PythonRundefkernel_step_with_shadow(state,wrp_id):new_state=kernel.step(state)wrp_event_store.append({"type":"WRP_KERNEL_STEP","wrp_id":wrp_id,"snapshot":new_state.model_dump()})returnnew_stateResult of Phase 2:✔ WRP is now causally aligned with execution✔ but still not controlling execution4. Phase 3 — WRP becomes primary runtime (CRITICAL SHIFT)This is where inversion happens:execution is now driven by WRP events, not internal logic4.1 Replace shell orchestration loopBEFORE (old shell):PythonRunkernel.step(state)AFTER (WRP-driven):PythonRundefruntime_loop(wrp_id):events=event_store.replay(wrp_id)state=snapshot_store.load(wrp_id)foreventinevents:ifnotwrp_validate(event):continuestate=wrp_kernel_bridge.apply_event(state,event)snapshot_store.save(state)4.2 Execution becomes event-triggeredInstead of:plan → execute → validateWe now have:WRP_PLANNED → triggers execution engineWRP_EXECUTED → triggers validation engineWRP_VALIDATED → triggers convergence checkResult of Phase 3:✔ WRP is now controlling flow✔ kernel becomes reactive✔ system is event-sourced end-to-end5. Phase 4 — Legacy collapse (removal of old system)Now we delete redundancy.5.1 Remove WorkStatus as active driverReplace all:PythonRunWorkStatuswith:PythonRunWRPStateor derived projection.5.2 Replace WorkflowState entirelyKeep only:PythonRunwork_status_to_phase()as compatibility shim.5.3 Remove direct transition tables from shellShell no longer owns lifecycle logic.It becomes:event router only5.4 Move execution authority fully to WRP runtimekernel is no longer called directlyonly triggered via WRP events6. Final dependency collapse (after migration)You end up with:Spring Boot (Ingress)↓WRP Event API↓Event Store (source of truth)↓WRP Runtime Engine↓Cognitive Kernel (pure compute)↓State Space + Policy Evolution↓Snapshot Store↓Nexus (observability only)7. What actually changed structurally (important)We fixed 3 deep architectural issues:7.1 BEFORE: dual truth problemWorkStatus (store)WorkflowState (IR)kernel state (runtime)❌ 3 competing state machines7.2 AFTER: single truthWRPState + event stream✔ one lifecycle authority✔ one transition system✔ one runtime protocol7.3 BEFORE: imperative executionKernel called directly.AFTER: event-driven executionKernel is:a projection over event history8. Migration order (VERY IMPORTANT)Do this in exact order:STEP 1Introduce WRP package (no integration)STEP 2Add shadow event emitters everywhereSTEP 3Persist WRP events in DBSTEP 4Build replay engineSTEP 5Switch shell runtime loop to WRP eventsSTEP 6Redirect kernel invocation to event bridgeSTEP 7Deprecate WorkStatus / WorkflowState usageSTEP 8Remove legacy transition system9. What you now have after full migrationYou have transformed LOSM into:afully event-sourced cognitive runtime governed by a unified lifecycle protocol (WRP)Which means:✔ deterministic replay✔ observable re