ythonRunscore(goal)=information_gain_estimate(goal)*novelty(goal)*structural_importance(goal)5. GOAL → ROVER TRANSLATIONThis is critical.Goals are not executed directly.They becomeRover constraints.5.1 translation ruleGoal → Directed Rover ProbeExample:JSON{"type":"resolve_anomaly","target":"node_42"}becomes:JSON{"signal_type":"targeted_probe","target":"node_42","depth":3,"reason":"resolve anomaly"}6. CLOSED LOOP ARCHITECTURE (FINAL FORM)Now the system is truly circular:Rover↓Absorb↓Nebula↓Memory MC↓Voyager↓Goal Engine↓Rover (directed)This is no longer pipeline architecture.It is:aself-referential exploration loop7. CRITICAL EMERGENT PROPERTYAt this stage, the system develops:“curiosity gradients”Meaning:it prefers uncertain regionsit prefers unresolved contradictionsit prefers high-information gain zonesNot because we told it to.But because:the goal function structurally rewards incompleteness8. SECOND-ORDER EFFECT: EXPLORATION MEMORYWe now track:JSON{"goal_id":"g12","generated_at":44,"resolved_at":51,"information_gain":0.73}So the system learns:which kinds of goals produce useful knowledge9. FEEDBACK INTO MEMORY CONSOLIDATIONMemory MC now uses goal history:goals that resolved well → stabilize concepts fasterfailed goals → mark regions as low-value exploration zonesSo consolidation becomesgoal-aware10. VOYAGER EVOLUTION (IMPORTANT)Voyager no longer just reasons.It now:evaluates goal relevancepredicts goal outcomescritiques goal structureSo it becomes:a meta-reasoning system over its own exploration strategy11. SYSTEM STATE (FINAL ARCHITECTURE)Rover        → perception + directed probesAbsorb       → structural graph builderNebula       → truth substrateMemory MC    → concept formation + compressionVoyager      → LLM-grounded reasoning + critiqueGoal Engine  → epistemic objective generatorVQL          → query languageCheckpoint   → event logReplay       → deterministic reconstructionFrames       → temporal graph viewVisualizer   → cognitive timeline UIStrontium    →