ODELWe define 3 temporal axes:2.1 Logical time (t)Checkpoint index:t = 0, 1, 2, ...2.2 Causal timeDependency order of events:Rover → Absorb → Commit → MC → Voyager2.3 Semantic timeWhen concepts stabilize or collapse.Example:node exists at t=3becomes “concept” at t=123. FRAME GENERATIONWe extend checkpoint replay:PythonRundefbuild_frames(checkpoints):nebula=Nebula()frames=[]forcpincheckpoints:apply_checkpoint(cp,nebula)frames.append(snapshot(nebula))returnframes3.1 Snapshot formatJSON{"t":42,"nodes": [...],"edges": [...],"concepts": [...],"metrics": {"node_count":120,"edge_count":340,"concept_count":12}}4. DIFF-BASED VISUALIZATION MODELInstead of rendering full graphs every frame:we render changes between frames4.1 delta computationPythonRundefdiff(frame_a,frame_b):return{"nodes_added":set(frame_b.nodes)-set(frame_a.nodes),"edges_added":set(frame_b.edges)-set(frame_a.edges),"concepts_formed":set(frame_b.concepts)-set(frame_a.concepts)}4.2 visual semanticsgreen = new nodeblue = stabilized conceptred = pruned nodeyellow = edge reinforcement(no colors required in implementation, just semantics)5. TIMELINE ENGINEWe define a navigation layer:play()pause()step_forward()step_backward()jump(t)5.1 rewind model (critical)PythonRundefrewind(frames,t):returnframes[:t]This enables:“what did the system believe at t=10?”“when did this concept emerge?”“what changed Voyager’s hypothesis?”6. CONCEPT EMERGENCE TRACKINGWe now explicitly track:“birth of concepts”JSON{"concept_id":"c12","first_seen":18,"stabilized_at":24,"source_nodes": ["n1","n2","n3"]}This is extremely important.It gives you:ontology evolution as a first-class signal7. VOYAGER INTEGRATION (TEMPORAL REASONING)Voyager now receives:JSON{"current_frame":42,"history_window": [35,41],"concept_evolution":true}So it can reason like:“this cluster was unstable earlier but stabilized”“this dependency only emerged after MC collapse”“this hypothesis was invalidated over time”8. MEMORY CONSOLIDATION VISUAL FEEDBACK LOOPMC now becomes