ay “continue”, I strongly recommendA next, because that’s where the system stops beingreactive cognitionand starts becomingself-directed cognition.SourcesYou said:continue, of courseChatGPT said:Good. Now we cross the last clean boundary in this architecture.Everything so far has been:perceptionstructurereasoningmemoryreplayvisualizationBut it is still missing one thing:intentSo we add it.This is:🎯 AUTONOMOUS GOAL FORMATION LAYER v0.1(how Strontium starts choosing what it wants to know next)0. CORE SHIFTUntil now:Rover decideswhat existsVoyager decideswhat it meansNow we introduce:a system that decideswhat is worth exploringNot externally defined tasks.Not user prompts.But internally generatedepistemic objectives.1. NEW SYSTEM COMPONENTGoal Engine (GE)Position:Rover → Absorb → Nebula → Memory MC → Voyager → Goal Engine → RoverThis closes the loop intoself-directed exploration.2. WHAT A GOAL ISA goal is not a task.A goal is:a structured hypothesis about missing knowledge in the graph2.1 Goal schemaJSON{"goal_id":"uuid","type":"reduce_uncertainty | explain_cluster | resolve_anomaly | expand_boundary","target": {"node_id":"optional","cluster_id":"optional"},"reason":"string","priority":0.0,"expected_information_gain":0.0}3. GOAL GENERATION SOURCESGoals are generated from 4 pressures:3.1 Uncertainty pressure (from Rover)low confidence nodes → exploration goals3.2 Compression pressure (from Memory MC)unstable clusters → stabilization goals3.3 Contradiction pressure (from Voyager)conflicting hypotheses → resolution goals3.4 Structural voids (from Nebula)unconnected regions → bridge goals4. GOAL GENERATION ENGINEWe formalize:PythonRundefgenerate_goals(nebula,voyager_output):goals=[]goals+=uncertainty_goals(nebula)goals+=compression_goals(nebula)goals+=contradiction_goals(voyager_output)goals+=structural_void_goals(nebula)returnrank(goals)4.1 ranking functionPythonRunscore(goal)=information_gain_estimate(goal)*novelty(goal)*structural_importance(goal)5. GOAL → ROVER TRANSLA