ering full graphs every frame:we render changes between frames4.1 delta computationPythonRundefdiff(frame_a,frame_b):return{"nodes_added":set(frame_b.nodes)-set(frame_a.nodes),"edges_added":set(frame_b.edges)-set(frame_a.edges),"concepts_formed":set(frame_b.concepts)-set(frame_a.concepts)}4.2 visual semanticsgreen = new nodeblue = stabilized conceptred = pruned nodeyellow = edge reinforcement(no colors required in implementation, just semantics)5. TIMELINE ENGINEWe define a navigation layer:play()pause()step_forward()step_backward()jump(t)5.1 rewind model (critical)PythonRundefrewind(frames,t):returnframes[:t]This enables:“what did the system believe at t=10?”“when did this concept emerge?”“what changed Voyager’s hypothesis?”6. CONCEPT EMERGENCE TRACKINGWe now explicitly track:“birth of concepts”JSON{"concept_id":"c12","first_seen":18,"stabilized_at":24,"source_nodes": ["n1","n2","n3"]}This is extremely important.It gives you:ontology evolution as a first-class signal7. VOYAGER INTEGRATION (TEMPORAL REASONING)Voyager now receives:JSON{"current_frame":42,"history_window": [35,41],"concept_evolution":true}So it can reason like:“this cluster was unstable earlier but stabilized”“this dependency only emerged after MC collapse”“this hypothesis was invalidated over time”8. MEMORY CONSOLIDATION VISUAL FEEDBACK LOOPMC now becomes visible in time:Before MC:many small nodesAfter MC:few stable concepts appear suddenlyThis creates:“semantic phase transitions”9. STRONTIUM UI MODEL (MINIMAL SPEC)We define a backend-neutral UI contract:JSON{"type":"timeline_graph_view","controls": {"playback":true,"frame_slider":true,"diff_view":true,"concept_highlighting":true},"data_source":"frames[]"}10. SYSTEM BEHAVIOR AFTER THIS LAYERNow the system is no longer just:runningstoringreasoningIt becomes:observable cognition over timeYou can now literally see:structure forminghypotheses shiftingconcepts stabilizingnoise being prunedattention drifting (Rover selection changes)11. EMERGENT PROPERTY (