ks.Not user prompts.But internally generatedepistemic objectives.1. NEW SYSTEM COMPONENTGoal Engine (GE)Position:Rover → Absorb → Nebula → Memory MC → Voyager → Goal Engine → RoverThis closes the loop intoself-directed exploration.2. WHAT A GOAL ISA goal is not a task.A goal is:a structured hypothesis about missing knowledge in the graph2.1 Goal schemaJSON{"goal_id":"uuid","type":"reduce_uncertainty | explain_cluster | resolve_anomaly | expand_boundary","target": {"node_id":"optional","cluster_id":"optional"},"reason":"string","priority":0.0,"expected_information_gain":0.0}3. GOAL GENERATION SOURCESGoals are generated from 4 pressures:3.1 Uncertainty pressure (from Rover)low confidence nodes → exploration goals3.2 Compression pressure (from Memory MC)unstable clusters → stabilization goals3.3 Contradiction pressure (from Voyager)conflicting hypotheses → resolution goals3.4 Structural voids (from Nebula)unconnected regions → bridge goals4. GOAL GENERATION ENGINEWe formalize:PythonRundefgenerate_goals(nebula,voyager_output):goals=[]goals+=uncertainty_goals(nebula)goals+=compression_goals(nebula)goals+=contradiction_goals(voyager_output)goals+=structural_void_goals(nebula)returnrank(goals)4.1 ranking functionPythonRunscore(goal)=information_gain_estimate(goal)*novelty(goal)*structural_importance(goal)5. GOAL → ROVER TRANSLATIONThis is critical.Goals are not executed directly.They becomeRover constraints.5.1 translation ruleGoal → Directed Rover ProbeExample:JSON{"type":"resolve_anomaly","target":"node_42"}becomes:JSON{"signal_type":"targeted_probe","target":"node_42","depth":3,"reason":"resolve anomaly"}6. CLOSED LOOP ARCHITECTURE (FINAL FORM)Now the system is truly circular:Rover↓Absorb↓Nebula↓Memory MC↓Voyager↓Goal Engine↓Rover (directed)This is no longer pipeline architecture.It is:aself-referential exploration loop7. CRITICAL EMERGENT PROPERTYAt this stage, the system develops:“curiosity gradients”Meaning:it prefers uncertain regionsit prefers unresolved contradict