y.This is:🧠 MEMORY CONSOLIDATION LAYER v0.1(turning raw graph growth into stable “concepts”)0. PURPOSEWe introduce a new subsystem:transform noisy, redundant, low-confidence graph structure intostable semantic unitsThis is where:“data” becomes “concepts”“clusters” become “entities”“repeated patterns” become durable memory1. NEW SYSTEM COMPONENTMemory Consolidator (MC)Position in pipeline:Rover → Absorb → Nebula → Voyager → Memory Consolidator → Nebula (updated)Important:this is the ONLY system allowed to rewrite or compress graph structure2. CONSOLIDATION TARGETSWe operate on 3 graph phenomena:2.1 Redundant nodesSame or near-same labels:ServiceBrokerservice-brokerService Broker2.2 Weak clustersDense subgraphs with:low confidence edgesrepetitive structureno external linkage2.3 High-frequency patternsRepeated structures across graph regions.3. CONSOLIDATION OPERATIONSWe define 4 transformations.3.1 MERGE (nodes → concept)PythonRundefmerge(nodes):return{"node_id":uuid(),"type":"concept","label":canonicalize(nodes),"members": [n["node_id"]forninnodes],"confidence":avg_confidence(nodes)}3.2 COLLAPSE (subgraph → single node)Used for dense clusters.A → B → C → D  (dense, repetitive)↓ClusterNode("PipelineChain")3.3 PRUNE (noise removal)PythonRundefprune(edges):return[eforeinedgesife["confidence"]>0.2]3.4 ABSTRACT (pattern → concept)This is the most important operation.Example:Repeated structure:A depends_on BB depends_on Cbecomes:Concept: "linear dependency chain"4. MEMORY CONSOLIDATION PIPELINE1. detect redundancy2. cluster nodes3. merge candidates4. collapse subgraphs5. prune weak edges6. emit abstract concepts7. write back to Nebula5. CLUSTER DETECTION (CORE MECHANISM)We define a simple first-pass heuristic:5.1 edge density clusteringPythonRundefdetect_clusters(nebula):clusters=[]visited=set()fornodeinnebula.nodes.values():ifnode["node_id"]invisited:continueneighborhood=expand_local(node,nebula)ifedge_density(neighborhood)>0.6:clusters.append(neighborhood)visited.update(