with multiple invokers: LocalInvoker (native language/framework dispatch) and Remote/HttpInvoker (network-mediated calls). This normalizes all brokers (Spring, Quarkus, Helidon, Go, Python) under a unified model where all brokers handle both LOCAL and REMOTE services as first-class citizens.\n\n### Requirements & Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] LOCAL redefined: co-located with and owned by broker runtime\n- [ ] ServiceDispatcher: unified dispatch across all brokers\n- [ ] LocalInvoker: native language/framework dispatch\n- [ ] RemoteInvoker: HTTP/network-mediated calls\n- [ ] All brokers handle LOCAL + REMOTE as first-class\n- [ ] Polyglot: Spring, Quarkus, Helidon, Go, Python unified model\n\n---\n	{nexus_service_broker_disambiguation,harvest,rover-batch,deepseek}	{"slug": "nexus_service_broker_disambiguation", "model": "DeepSeek V4 (manual extraction)", "source_chat": "Nexus - Service Broker Disambiguation", "has_source_text": true}	2026-06-21 05:59:52.398586+00	2026-06-21 05:59:52.398586+00	2026-06-21 05:59:52.398586+00	9999-12-31 23:59:59+00
