ntent_description": "(1) Active entities — what is tracked. (2) Open structures — plans, issues, clusters. (3) Attention anchors — high-salience unresolved questions, recent reflection outputs. Each may have different decay functions.", "implementation_notes": []}, {"title": "Day/Night Cycle as Perceptual Update Mechanism", "status": "Agreed", "requirements": ["Day ops must not require full perceptual recalculation", "Night ops reconcile evidence into revised belief state"], "code_snippets": [], "open_questions": ["What triggers night? Time-based, event-based, or both?"], "intent_description": "Day = evidence accumulation only (no full perceptual recalculation). Night = reflection/perceptual update cycle where belief state is recomputed. Without reflection, perception freezes.", "implementation_notes": []}]	\N	{deepseek-v4,harvest,operational_intelligence_loop}	{"model": "DeepSeek V4", "ollama_url": "agent-in-the-loop (manual inference)", "total_chunks": 1, "failed_chunks": 0, "successful_chunks": 1}	2026-06-21 03:17:05.762557+00	2026-06-21 03:17:05.762557+00	2026-06-21 03:17:05.762557+00	9999-12-31 23:59:59+00
